{
  "_comment": [
    "Burning Sun Dark — generated by dotfiles/theme/build.sh, do not edit.",
    "Monochrome and rubrication: the interface reads in grey, and vermilion is",
    "spent on the things that need finding — errors, permission prompts, the",
    "active mode. Subagent colours and diffs keep a distinction because",
    "removing it there would destroy meaning rather than noise."
  ],
  "name": "Burning Sun Dark",
  "_base_comment": [
    "dark-ansi / light-ansi, not dark / light. Inline `code` is rendered by a",
    "path that reads the BASE palette and ignores `overrides`, so with a plain",
    "dark base it stays rgb(177,185,249) — a periwinkle blue — no matter what",
    "we set. The -ansi bases spell that slot as ansi:blue / ansi:blueBright,",
    "which resolves through the terminal's own palette, and ours is grey.",
    "Every other token is overridden below, so the base only shows through on",
    "the paths that ignore overrides."
  ],
  "base": "dark-ansi",
  "overrides": {
    "background": "#0a0a0a",
    "text": "#ede8e0",
    "inverseText": "#0a0a0a",
    "subtle": "#3b3835",
    "inactive": "#5f5a52",
    "inactiveShimmer": "#817b71",

